# Line endings. The repo's default `core.autocrlf=true` turns every text file
# into CRLF in the working tree on Windows, which silently breaks the golden
# fixtures below: they are compared byte-for-byte against what the writer
# produces, so a CRLF checkout fails those tests on a machine where nothing is
# actually wrong.
#
# `-text` (binary) on the fixtures means "check out and commit exactly these
# bytes", which is what a byte-exact golden needs. Everything else keeps the
# normal autocrlf behaviour.
src-tauri/tests/fixtures/** -text

# Scripts run under Git Bash / a POSIX shell on every platform; CRLF in them
# breaks `#!/bin/bash` and here-documents.
*.sh text eol=lf
